-- title:
--   Valuation rings over A dominating R₀ are Igusa rings, q=3
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=3$, let $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$, in the sense that $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` — the subfield of Laurent series over the residue field of $A$ generated by the $j$-expansion and its level-$M'$ substitute — over that residue field, whose members are exactly the supersingular places: the rational affine geometric places at which the geometric $j$-invariant takes a supersingular value. Assume the base-changed level-$M'$ modular function field $F_{M'}=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is contained in $F=$ `fieldBar q M'`, the function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ with $H\le(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, both realised inside Laurent series. Let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of $F_{M'}$ along $A$ with values in `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of $F_{M'}$ meeting $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in $A$, a surjective residue map onto that field with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with the residue map of $A$ on constants, together with a degree-preserving map on places compatible with orders of divisors; assume moreover that $R_0$ is pinned to coefficientwise reduction, namely every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image lies in $F_{M'}$ belongs to `R₀.integers` and has residue the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $\zeta$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and let $\ell\mapsto\mathcal O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_\ell$ assign to each point of $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ a valuation subring of $F$ such that at the point $[1:0]$ it is the Gauss ring of quotients $x/y$ of Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ whose denominator has nonzero coefficientwise reduction, and such that for every $\ell$ there is $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\subset\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ whose reduction modulo $q$ carries $[1:0]$ to $\ell$ and with $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_\ell$ the pullback of $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_{[1:0]}$ along the level automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` of $F$. Finally let $\mathcal O$ be a valuation subring of $F$ whose intersection with $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is $A$, in the sense that for $x\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ the image of $x$ in $F$ lies in $\mathcal O$ exactly when $x\in A$, and such that every element of `R₀.integers` maps into $\mathcal O$. Then $\mathcal O=\mathcal O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_\ell$ for some $\ell\in\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$.
--
--   This is the classification, for $q=3$, of the valuation rings of the full-level function field which lie over the given valuation ring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ above $q$ and dominate the good-reduction ring of the level-$M'$ field: they are precisely the $q+1$ Igusa rings attached to the points of $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$. It feeds the identification of the Igusa components in the semistable model of the full-level curve at $q=3$ and, through that, the construction of the charts, annuli and node data used there.
